module lib/hf/tests/orthogonalize
  The checks of lib/hf/orthogonalize against reference data, and their helpers.

orth_t_opts  @7a982dab
  why    The tests pick members by number.
  k      the orthogonalizer member

orth_t_core  @51d5ffc1
  why    The SCF's answer must not depend on the orthogonalizer or the
         eigensolver: the eigenvalues of the core Hamiltonian and the
         density of its lowest orbitals are compared across all of them
         [test "on water's core Hamiltonian the eigensolvers agree, and so do the orthogonalizers"].
  H      the core Hamiltonian, `[n, n]`
  S      the overlap matrix, `[n, n]`
  k      the orthogonalizer member
  nocc   how many orbitals are occupied
  o      the options with orthogonalizer k
  X      its orthogonalizer
  Xm     its kept columns, `[n, m]`
  Hp     `X^T H X`, `[m, m]`
  R      `eig_ql`'s eigenvalues and eigenvectors of Hp
  C      the occupied orbitals on the original basis, `[n, nocc]`

  = Hp     the core Hamiltonian in this orthogonalizer's basis
  = C      the occupied orbitals on the original basis: `C C^T`, the projector returned, does not depend on X
